cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use MintMap in research or a report, please cite it as below."
title: "MintMap: a reviewed map of every code path that creates a login session or credential in a Django app, enforced in CI"
type: software
authors:
  - name: "MintMap contributors"
    website: "https://github.com/mohamedmoatazsec/mintmap/graphs/contributors"
version: "0.6.0a1"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/mohamedmoatazsec/mintmap"
url: "https://github.com/mohamedmoatazsec/mintmap"
abstract: >-
  MintMap is a static-analysis tool for Django projects. It finds the code paths that create a login session or
  credential, stores them in a human-reviewed lock file, and fails continuous integration when that set, or the
  code on it, changes. Its miss rate and false-alarm rate were measured on projects it was not developed against
  and are published with the tool.
keywords:
  - django
  - security
  - authentication
  - static analysis
  - continuous integration
